# --- V21 Phase 1 (Core Freeze) — Period Lock Enforcement -------------------
#
# `PERIOD_LOCK_ENFORCE=true` activates the canonical period-lock guard
# inside `DoubleEntryJournalService.appendBalanced`. When ON:
#
#   • Journal writes targeting a CLOSED financial period are REFUSED
#     with `ConflictException` AND an audit row is written to
#     `FinancialPeriodViolation`.
#   • Reversal entries (`allowReversal=true`) bypass the refusal but
#     are still audited.
#   • Idempotent retries of an EXISTING `sourceRef` short-circuit
#     without throwing, even on a CLOSED period (the original write
#     happened while the period was OPEN).
#
# Production rollout MUST follow `docs/architecture/operational-runbooks/
# period-lock-enforcement.md`:
#
#   1. Run the system in monitor mode (`PERIOD_LOCK_ENFORCE` unset
#      OR `false`) for one full month-end cycle.
#   2. Inspect `[FINANCIAL_PERIOD_VIOLATION]` log lines + the
#      `FinancialPeriodViolation` table; classify legitimate writes
#      vs bugs.
#   3. Once violations are zero (or all are known reversals), set
#      `PERIOD_LOCK_ENFORCE=true` and roll the deployment.
#
# Disable: set `PERIOD_LOCK_ENFORCE=false` and roll the deployment.
# Historical violation rows are append-only; they remain.
#
# PERIOD_LOCK_ENFORCE=true

# --- Fail-closed journaling for CRITICAL wrappers -------------------------
#
# `JOURNAL_FAIL_CLOSED_CRITICAL=true` makes the two highest-frequency
# money-movement journal wrappers fail-closed:
#   - appendExternalPaymentEntrySafe (cash / KNET / payment-link)
#   - appendInvoiceIssuanceEntrySafe (invoice issuance)
#
# When ON: if the journal write fails (after period-lock re-throw and
# P2002 idempotency recovery, and AFTER the failure is logged +
# persisted to JournalFailureLog), the original error is re-thrown so
# the surrounding business $transaction ROLLS BACK — no payment /
# invoice is committed without its matching journal entry.
#
# When unset / not `true`: legacy fail-open behaviour (swallow + trip
# circuit breaker + return null). Flip to `true`/remove to roll back
# instantly without a code change. The other `*Safe` wrappers are NOT
# affected by this flag.
# JOURNAL_FAIL_CLOSED_CRITICAL=true

# Database
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DATABASE"
# Local Docker (`docker compose up -d` in repo root; see `docker-compose.yml`):
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:password123@127.0.0.1:5432/safari_erp_dev"
# Keep Railway/production URL in `.env.railway` (gitignored) — never point daily dev at Railway.
# `scripts/reset-invoices.ts` with `--confirm=...` requires explicit consent:
# RESET_ALLOW_LOCAL=true       — allow wipe when DATABASE_URL is localhost / Docker postgres
# RESET_ALLOW_NON_LOCAL=true   — allow wipe when DATABASE_URL is remote (e.g. Railway)

# Nest HTTP port (defaults to 3000 in `src/main.ts`). Must match the Vite dev proxy target in `web/.env` (`API_PROXY_TARGET`, default `http://127.0.0.1:3000`) or SafariStream / `/api` calls will show ECONNREFUSED.
# PORT=3000
#
# Local API: use `npm run dev` or `npm run start:dev` (Nest compiles TS on the fly).
# `npm run start` runs **compiled** `dist/main.js` only — after pulling changes run `npm run build` or `npm run dist:start`, or new routes (e.g. GET /api/customers/:id/360) will 404 with "Cannot GET …".
# Optional: `DISABLE_SPA_STATIC=1` skips SPA from the API process (when `web/dist` exists) to isolate routing issues.
# DISABLE_SPA_STATIC=1

# JWT — one HMAC secret for staff access tokens, INVOICE_SHARE, and
# /api/public/invoice/* (PDF). Production (Render) must set a long random
# value; keep it stable across deploys. If `invoicePdfUrl` 404s or Moatmt
# shows a ~0.5KB attachment, the token was signed with a different `JWT_SECRET`.
JWT_SECRET=change-me

# --- Auth session lifecycle (V24+) ---
# Access-token TTL is read from `AUTH_ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL`. The code default
# is `24h` (raised from `15m` in V24+ so an operator can keep one tab
# open through a full working day without the SSE/dashboard streams
# being torn down by a 401). Override here if you want a different
# window (e.g. `15m` to test the silent-refresh path locally, or `12h`
# for a tighter security posture). The refresh-token rotation contract
# is unchanged: refresh tokens live `AUTH_REFRESH_TOKEN_DAYS` days
# (default 7) and rotate on every use; replay revokes the entire family.
# AUTH_ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL=24h
# AUTH_REFRESH_TOKEN_DAYS=7

# Auth hashing workers. Production should keep at least 1 worker; local/k6
# troubleshooting can lower this if bcrypt worker starvation appears.
# BCRYPT_WORKERS=2
# BCRYPT_ROUNDS=12

# --- Banking core read/write flags ---
# Final ledger mode makes JournalEntry/JournalLine the canonical read source
# for AR/debt and implicitly enables V20_3_TRUE_ACCOUNTING + USE_JOURNAL_AS_SOURCE.
# Production should keep these aligned unless intentionally running a canary.
# V20_4_FINAL_LEDGER=true
# V20_3_TRUE_ACCOUNTING=true
# USE_JOURNAL_AS_SOURCE=true
#
# When true, new PAYMENT_LINK / ONLINE orders immediately register AR debt
# (CustomerWallet.debt + Journal AR 1300) at order creation, before payment.
# PAYMENT_LINK_IMMEDIATE_DEBT=true

# CORS (comma-separated origins). Local dev example:
# CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173
#
# Production on Render — copy from deploy/render-production.env into the dashboard, or use:
# CORS_ORIGIN=https://safariomni.com,https://www.safariomni.com
# PUBLIC_API_URL=https://safariomni.com
# PAYMENTS_CALLBACK_PUBLIC_URL=https://safariomni.com
# PUBLIC_WEB_APP_URL=https://safariomni.com
#
# If the API runs on a separate host (e.g. api.safariomni.com), use that for PUBLIC_API_URL and PAYMENTS_CALLBACK_PUBLIC_URL instead,
# and ensure CORS_ORIGIN still lists the browser origins above.

# --- UPayments Kuwait Gateway (hosted payment link + webhook) ---
# Provider: https://developers.upayments.com/reference/overview
#
# Base URL of the UPayments API (no trailing slash).
#   Production: https://apiv2api.upayments.com
#   Sandbox:    https://sandboxapi.upayments.com
# Note: api.upayments.com is the merchant dashboard domain, NOT the API
# (/api/v1/charge there returns the dashboard's 404 HTML). Use apiv2api.
# Leave EMPTY to run the in-process mock checkout page (local dev only).
# Production MUST set this + PAYMENTS_API_KEY; otherwise every ONLINE order
# gets /api/payments/mock-checkout?orderId=… instead of a real UPayments link.
PAYMENTS_API_BASE_URL=
# Set to true/1/yes to force mock links even if PAYMENTS_API_BASE_URL is set
# (testing only; never in production if you need real UPayments).
# PAYMENTS_MOCK=
# Optional: ms for fetch to UPayments (default 60000). Raise if you see ETIMEDOUT on slow networks.
# PAYMENTS_UPAYMENTS_TIMEOUT_MS=90000

# UPayments API key (Bearer token). Get from merchant dashboard →
# Payment Gateway → API Credentials. Separate keys for prod vs sandbox.
PAYMENTS_API_KEY=

# Merchant ID on the UPayments account. Informational only — not
# sent on every request but kept for support/audit parity with the
# dashboard.
PAYMENTS_MERCHANT_ID=

# Legacy HMAC secret (kept for non-UPayments gateways + devMock
# signature fallback). UPayments itself is verified via
# Server-to-Server inquiry, so this is optional when PAYMENTS_API_BASE_URL
# points at UPayments. Required when NODE_ENV=production and ANY
# non-UPayments gateway is pointed at /api/payments/callback.
PAYMENTS_SECRET=

# Public HTTPS base URL of THIS backend (no trailing slash), used
# to build the notificationUrl (webhook) we hand to UPayments:
#   {PAYMENTS_CALLBACK_PUBLIC_URL}/api/payments/callback
PAYMENTS_CALLBACK_PUBLIC_URL=

# Fallback if PAYMENTS_CALLBACK_PUBLIC_URL is unset (e.g. local dev).
PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Customer-facing return + cancel URLs are derived from PUBLIC_WEB_APP_URL
# (declared below): `${PUBLIC_WEB_APP_URL}/payment/success|failed?orderId=…`
# so make sure that variable points at the actual SPA origin (not the
# API host) in production.

# --- Operating hours (Kuwait) — blocks POST/PUT/PATCH outside window for API clients ---
# false or 0 = lock off (24/7) — e.g. local dev or temporary production override.
# Use plain `false` (lowercase) in Render; any other value = lock on.
# When off: no mutating-API block (middleware) AND DRIVER/MANAGER can log in any hour.
# true (default) = enforce OPERATING_HOURS_KUWAIT_* in Asia/Kuwait.
OPERATING_HOURS_LOCK_ENABLED=true
# Emergency login outside hours without disabling full lock: AUTH_BYPASS_WORKING_HOURS=true
OPERATING_HOURS_KUWAIT_START_HOUR=7
OPERATING_HOURS_KUWAIT_END_HOUR=23

# --- Customer notify (async after POS invoice) — Moatmt (مؤتمت) WhatsApp send layer ---
# When MOATMT_INSTANCE_ID + MOATMT_ACCESS_TOKEN are set, the API POSTs to {MOATMT_API_BASE_URL}/send
# (default base: https://moatmt.sa/api). On Moatmt failure, CUSTOMER_NOTIFY_WEBHOOK_URL is used if set.
#
# Number format in JSON field `number` (string): 965 + 8 digits, e.g. "96551234567".
#   Stored customer values like 51234567, +965 5123 4567, 00965… are normalized the same.
#   Invalid Kuwait mobile → send skipped; check server logs: [Moatmt] and "invalid Kuwait mobile".
#
# MOATMT_API_BASE_URL=https://moatmt.sa/api
# MOATMT_INSTANCE_ID=          # from Moatmt panel (no extra quotes in production env UI)
# MOATMT_ACCESS_TOKEN=         # long API token from Moatmt (often 32+ chars); 10–20 char values are usually wrong
# Optional: MOATMT_OMIT_QUERY_AUTH=1 — omit access_token&instance_id from URL (still adds `number` to query + full JSON body).
# If JSON keeps returning "Access token is required" but your token is long, try: MOATMT_FORCE_FORM=1
#
# type=media (PDF) vs type=text: only `1` or `true` (case-insensitive) enable media; `0` / `false` / unset = text only.
# MOATMT_USE_INVOICE_MEDIA=0
# V19.27.4 — when media is off, invoice text defaults to minimal (رقم + إجمالي 3dp + رابط دفع). Set to 0 to use the long template.
# MOATMT_INVOICE_MINIMAL_TEXT=0
# Optional — use type=media with public invoice URL (media_url must be a direct file URL; many SPA/HTML URLs fail to fetch)
# MOATMT_USE_INVOICE_MEDIA=1
# MOATMT_MEDIA_CAPTION=فاتورتك مرفقة 👇
# MOATMT_EDIT_MEDIA_CAPTION=نسخة محدثة 👇
# MOATMT_INVOICE_MEDIA_FILENAME=invoice.png
#
# --- Manual test (Postman or curl) — same JSON shape as the app (replace placeholders) ---
# export MOATMT_API_BASE_URL=https://moatmt.sa/api
# export INST=your_instance_id
# export TOK=your_access_token
# export NUM=96551234567
# curl -sS -X POST "${MOATMT_API_BASE_URL}/send" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d "{\"number\":\"$NUM\",\"type\":\"text\",\"message\":\"اختبار مؤتمت من curl\",\"instance_id\":\"$INST\",\"access_token\":\"$TOK\"}"
# Expect: HTTP 2xx; check response body. Logs on the app use lines [Moatmt] request → / response ← for every attempt.
#
# Optional integrator — POST JSON { to, message, orderId, template, invoiceShareUrl?, invoiceShareItems? }
# After branch/driver checkout, `message` includes a signed /public/invoice/:token link when PUBLIC_WEB_APP_URL is set.
CUSTOMER_NOTIFY_WEBHOOK_URL=
# Optional — same POST shape; used first for staff when a CC supervisor edits a POS invoice (to=`User.phone` of issuer; template=invoice_edited_issuer). Falls back to CUSTOMER_NOTIFY_WEBHOOK_URL if unset.
STAFF_INVOICE_NOTIFY_WEBHOOK_URL=

# --- System Guardian — autonomous platform watcher + WhatsApp alerts ---
# The Guardian sweeps every SYSTEM_GUARDIAN_INTERVAL_MS (default 5min) and
# notifies the OWNER on WhatsApp when a CRITICAL issue is detected (or a
# WARNING persists across consecutive sweeps). It re-uses the existing
# Moatmt gateway (MOATMT_INSTANCE_ID + MOATMT_ACCESS_TOKEN) and falls back
# to SYSTEM_GUARDIAN_WEBHOOK_URL → CUSTOMER_NOTIFY_WEBHOOK_URL → log.
#
# Owner phone (Kuwait E.164 format, with or without leading +): default 96591111855
SYSTEM_GUARDIAN_OWNER_PHONE=96591111855
# Sweep period in ms. Minimum 30s (lower values are clamped to the default).
# SYSTEM_GUARDIAN_INTERVAL_MS=300000
# Set to 0 to disable the scheduled sweep entirely (the manual /run endpoint still works).
# SYSTEM_GUARDIAN_ENABLED=1
# Optional — outbound JSON webhook used when Moatmt is unavailable. POST shape:
#   { "to": "9659xxxxxxx", "message": "🚨 SYSTEM ALERT …", "template": "system_guardian_alert" }
# SYSTEM_GUARDIAN_WEBHOOK_URL=
# API latency threshold (ms) — exceeding this triggers a WARNING. Default 4000.
# Tighten in production where Postgres co-locates with the API (1500-2000 is realistic).
# SYSTEM_GUARDIAN_API_LATENCY_WARN_MS=4000

# Public web app URL for payment return URLs + automatic customer receipt links (no trailing slash).
# CRITICAL for UPayments: createPaymentLink sends returnUrl/cancelUrl = `${PUBLIC_WEB_APP_URL}/payment/success|failed?...`.
# If this stays localhost on a production server, the customer pays on the phone then Safari opens "localhost" and cannot connect;
# the money may leave the card but the order can stay unpaid until the webhook (notificationUrl) is also wrong — see
# PAYMENTS_CALLBACK_PUBLIC_URL. Production: set to your real site, e.g. https://www.safariomni.com (see deploy/render-production.env).
PUBLIC_WEB_APP_URL=http://localhost:5173

# --- V10/V11 storage & seed (staging) ---
# STORAGE_DRIVER=local
# SEED_FORCE_CANONICAL_FEES=true

# --- Stage-G — Observability (Sentry) ---
# Backend DSN. Leave empty to disable Sentry (local dev default).
SENTRY_DSN=
# Git SHA or semver for release-tag tie-in. Optional but recommended.
SENTRY_RELEASE=
# Fraction of transactions to trace (0.0–1.0). Defaults to 0.1 when unset.
SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE=0.1

# --- Stage-G — /api/health tuning ---
# Alert thresholds used by /api/health (MB). 503 is returned when exceeded.
HEALTH_HEAP_LIMIT_MB=300
HEALTH_RSS_LIMIT_MB=500

# --- Stage-G — Backup script (see scripts/pg-backup.sh + docs/BACKUP.md) ---
# BACKUP_DIR=/var/backups/safari-erp
# BACKUP_RETENTION_DAYS=14

# --- Stage-G — Migration drift guard (scripts/check-migration-drift.ts) ---
# Used by `npm run db:check-drift` for CI-time schema vs. migrations
# comparison. Must point at an empty throwaway Postgres database.
# SHADOW_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/shadow_db"

# --- Prepaid wallet auto-reconcile (V19.13.1) ---
# Set to `true` to disable the every-15-min cron that pays UNPAID invoices
# from positive CustomerWallet.balance (FIFO). Default: cron runs.
# PREPAID_AUTO_RECONCILE_CRON_DISABLED=true
